package cron

import "log/slog"

// Deps is the dependency bundle every scheduled job receives.
//
// It is the seam for handing jobs what they need without a service locator: add
// a field per dependency your jobs use — an events publisher, a repository, a
// mailer — and construct it in internal/di/cron_provider.go's NewCronDeps, which
// Loom supplies. A job reads the bundle from its second parameter:
//
//	func Register(s *Scheduler) error {
//		return s.Register("nightly-report", "0 3 * * *", func(ctx context.Context, deps *Deps) {
//			deps.Logger.Info("nightly report started")
//		})
//	}
//
// The bundle ships with the logger, the one dependency every job can use. The
// scheduler guarantees the pointer it hands a job is never nil, so a job that
// needs nothing can ignore it; a bundle built by a bare New has a nil Logger, so
// a job that logs should still guard it or rely on the graph. Keep this type
// stable: internal/cron references it and internal/di/cron_provider.go
// constructs it.
type Deps struct {
	// Logger is the graph's logger, so a job logs through the one logging
	// protocol the process owns.
	Logger *slog.Logger
}
